xvfb: synchronize DRI3 presents explicitly with timeline syncobjs

A DRI3 client's frame reaches this server's screen only as a Present copy
that glamor queues on its own context, and the server learns nothing of when
the client's rendering into the pixmap completes or tells the client when
the copy has read it. Implicit fences on the dmabuf close both gaps where a
driver attaches them; the NVIDIA driver attaches none, and presents from its
Vulkan driver land out of order: a frame shows a swapchain image as it was
one cycle before or after.

- glamor imports DRI3 1.4 timeline syncobjs on its render node where the
  kernel has them and the eventfd ioctl to wait on them with, and EGL can
  fence the work glamor queues (EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync).
- Present's screen mode takes explicitly synchronized pixmaps, and reports
  PresentCapabilitySyncobj, on a screen whose renderer fences its copies:
  the copy waits for the acquire point and its fence signals the release
  point, through the code the window mode shares. A screen without a driver
  of its own answers for its windows, which sit on no CRTC.
- Xvfb gives Present the fenced flush once the extension has set up the
  screen.

